  "guide.desk.body": "Clock, music, weather, load and screen time live on the wallpaper. In edit mode you drag them, scroll to resize, and switch each one between its faces.",
  "guide.desk.title": "Desktop widgets",
  "guide.finish": "done",
  "guide.hello.body": "Everything here is one Quickshell config: the bar, the panels, the lock screen, the sounds. Every optional part can be switched off in the settings.",
  "guide.hello.title": "Your shell",
  "guide.next": "next",
  "guide.panels.body": "Nothing is on screen until you ask for it: launcher, window overview, clipboard history, network, music. Escape closes whatever is open.",
  "guide.panels.title": "Panels",
  "guide.quick.body": "The handle on the right edge opens into drawing on the screen, a timer, current load and the dock. Drag the handle itself to move it out of the way.",
  "guide.quick.title": "Quick actions",
  "guide.time.body": "Notifications are kept even while silenced, so nothing is lost to do-not-disturb. Screen time is counted per application and never leaves this machine.",
